Let the repository-info endpoint skip the HF `siblings` list.

GET /api/{repo_type}s/{namespace}/{name} always materialises the full
HuggingFace `siblings` array. For a 40k-file dataset that is a 6 MB
response whose TTFB is ~0.93 s (41 sequential lakeFS list_objects pages
plus the per-object bookkeeping), and the SPA does not read
repoInfo.siblings at all — it builds its tree from /tree/. Because
RepoViewer's onMounted awaits loadRepoInfo() before loadFileTree() and
loadReadme(), that response blocks the dataset card (README) even though
the README itself is a 5 KB, ~35 ms fetch.

Add an `include_siblings` query parameter (default true) so the SPA can
ask for the cheap metadata-only response. The default preserves the
existing wire shape for `huggingface_hub` clients, which is why this is
opt-in rather than a behaviour change.

